#4471 is marked known as one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The export does not
support that. Its 412 unique reports split into two causes, and the parser fix leaves 33 of
them broken.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. <code>parser</code> covers 379 reports; <code>hint</code> covers 33. The 33 have
no ticket of their own.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The desk counted 412 reports. The export holds 427 rows because 15 ids appear twice;
`uniqueById` drops the repeats.

## The two tickets

- **[#1 · Parser reads dates month first](https://github.com/dkey1994macmini1/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)**
  covers **379 reports** from all 11 tenants on file, across app, email and booking-v2. The shared
  parser ignores the tenant's locale.
- **[#2 · booking-v3 hint prints MM/DD/YYYY](https://github.com/dkey1994macmini1/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)**
  covers **33 reports**, all from day-first tenants on booking-v3 forms. The hint says month
  first; the form reads day first.

## Why subject dedupe missed it

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. These two
causes share subjects such as "Date is wrong", so the reports landed in one ticket.
`meta.intakeTag` did not catch it either: it is a guess from the reporter's browser, not the
tenant's locale. In this export 23 parser reports are tagged `hint` and 15 hint reports are
tagged `parser`.

## Five reports that read as a one-day move

R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 describe a one-day shift rather than a swapped
month and day. They stay counted under `parser`, as `desk-notes.json` says, so the two tickets
still add up to 412. They are a note on the parser ticket, not a third ticket.

## What changes

Split #4471 into the two tickets above. Keep the parser ticket as the known issue and open the 33
form reports as their own. Re-read the merged report after both fixes ship.

